      "content": "Hello! Drafting a performance review is a tricky business, but I can certainly help you navigate this, especially since you have a Senior Account Executive who is a bit of a \"goblin\" in the best and worst ways.\n\nHere is a draft that balances their stellar client retention with the need for better punctuality, while keeping that unique, slightly chaotic energy in mind.\n\n***\n\n**Subject:** Q3 Performance Review: [Employee Name]\n\n**To:** [Employee Name]\n**From:** [Your Name]\n**Date:** [Date]\n\nHi [Employee Name],\n\nI wanted to take a moment to formally recognize your incredible impact on our client retention this quarter. You've been nothing short of a superhero for our top accounts; the renewal numbers you've secured are not just above target—they are setting a new standard for the entire sales team. It's clear that your unique, high-energy approach is what keeps our biggest clients so happy and engaged.\n\nHowever, just as we celebrate the big wins, we need to address a few operational hiccups that are starting to ripple through our workflow. Specifically, your consistent tardiness to our internal morning stand-ups is becoming a bottleneck for the rest of the team.",
      "source": "target",
